{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/925091-what-people-would-you-use-as-examples-for-the-strength-attribute","id":925091,"title":"what people would you use as examples for the strength attribute??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-02T16:28:33-07:00","id":925091,"title":"what people would you use as examples for the strength attribute??","content":"1 to 5 both male and female if possible. i don't really know how strength works biologically. for instance i was told that bruce lee would be stronger than a bodybuilder so i assume he would be strength 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:03:28-07:00","id":925105,"title":"","content":"Don't most games have a feat of strength chart that gives Max weight lifted between strength 1 - 10","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T21:32:09-07:00","id":925198,"title":"","content":"That they do.. Heck, iirc in werewolf, the chart goes up through 10, to account for the changing forms and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T00:48:41-07:00","id":926314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/925091-what-people-would-you-use-as-examples-for-the-strength-attribute#post925091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 to 5 both male and female if possible. i don't really know how strength works biologically. for instance i was told that bruce lee would be stronger than a bodybuilder so i assume he would be strength 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>This entirely depends on your definition of Strength. Strength is a very nebulous and its application within the system is mandated by its pairing with an ability. This is necessary due to the fact that Strength as such is an abstraction. In the real world a marathon runner, a sprint runner, a weight lifter and a martial artist are all very strong people, but none of them can actually do what the others can. So just if Usain Bolt can run circles and break records around a weightlifrer does not mean that he can lift as much as the weightlifter can.<br /> <br /> So, use the charts, couple it with skills and remember that it's an abstraction of complex biological mechanics that are not as simple in the real world as they are in a game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}